   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Smoke Dissolve\n\nA ring of smoke expands from the center of the frame and the incoming scene materializes out of it. Rebuilt with a deterministic Canvas 2D noise field instead of the original WebGL shader. The block draws its own colored field between two built-in placeholder scenes A and B (the two .smd-panel elements); to use it between your own scenes, replace the contents of those two panels and keep the block on a track above.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 3.4667 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A moody, atmospheric reveal where the next scene should emerge from the middle of the frame.\n- Slow chapter breaks with a lot of runtime.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Fast cuts or upbeat promos: the smoke needs time to read.\n- Repeated use in one video.\n\nVariables:\n- color_back (color): Background, default \"#141318\"\n- color (color): Smoke color, default \"#8f88ae\"\n- speed (number, 0-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
